= Additional lead: a pole-independent differential filter
#image("differential-lead60.svg",width:100%)
PROPOSED, not measured: for a separable ordinary target map, the pullback
of dx/x is a nonzero holomorphic logarithmic differential. Cartier fixes
it; sigma(x)=x also makes it sigma-fixed. Compute the complete joint fixed
space on all61 source differentials before enumerating every pole bound.
A zero joint space would exclude this separable compatible-map class at
all bounds; a nonzero space constrains rational-function reconstruction.

The source still needs the complete divisor of a separating du, every
exceptional branch, an actual61-form basis and complete whole-field square
decompositions f=g squared+u h squared. Construct the true Cartier and
sigma matrices; expand inverse squaring on F32 coefficients, c maps to
c^16, into305 binary coordinates. Solve the complete F2 joint kernel.
Do not treat this semilinear fixed set as an F32-linear space.

A differential direction alone does not supply x, an elliptic map or
order11 action. Recover d(x)=x omega modulo squares, prescribed divisors,
the AS relation, all5 conjugates and the intended factor/action separately.
Inseparable maps require justified Frobenius removal before this gate.
The cubic enlargement and other original leads remain on the worklist.

Primary source checked: Friedlander, Garton, Malmskog, Pries and Weir,
The a-numbers of Jacobians of Suzuki curves, section3.3, gives the standard
Cartier rules and square-decomposition formula. Its Suzuki-specific basis
and matrices are not transferred here. Source:
#link("https://www.math.colostate.edu/~pries/Preprints/13AMSSummerSuzukiFinal.pdf")[Author preprint, section3.3].
